### S1 | type: add | dimension: constructor | symbol: entity_description
- Needs: n1/n2 (t1:s1), n9 (t2:s6), n11 (t2:s8), n14 (t2:s14), n15 (t2:s16); qualified lettuce and one selected sliced piece.
- Searches tried: search "entity description spatial location state portion slice", "single piece of sliced material", "object description state sliced location"; widen "describe an entity with sliced-piece quantity and spatial location" and the corresponding action needs; closest entries lexical_label (no properties), state_sliced (a condition, not a piece), spatial_constraint (constraint rather than qualified referent), has_state/spatial_state (assertions), location_spec (geographical qualifiers).
- Typed parameters: base: TERM, state?: STRING, piece?: BOOL, count?: NUMBER, location?: TERM, relation?: STRING.
- Interpretation: Describes an entity of the base kind, optionally qualified by state and spatial location; piece=TRUE selects pieces of that base material and count specifies their number, not the number of whole source entities. count is a positive integer; state is a governed state-value; location/relation must occur together and relation is a governed spatial-relation; omission leaves a qualifier unspecified; construction asserts nothing and creates no runtime identity.
- Example: A lexical_label(food_label::lettuce) passed as base with state=state_sliced, piece=TRUE, count=1 describes one lettuce slice; the same base with location=counter_term, relation=on describes the lettuce on the counter.
- Contrast: A state_sliced description without piece=TRUE/count=1 does not specify a single selected slice; this constructor neither slices nor claims that slicing occurred.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"entity_description","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM entity_description(base: TERM, state?: STRING, piece?: BOOL, count?: NUMBER, location?: TERM, relation?: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Nonasserting qualified entity description: base identifies its kind/material; state is a state-value; piece=TRUE denotes pieces of that material and count is a positive integer counting the selected entities/pieces. Spatial qualification requires both location: an entity/location description, and relation: a spatial-relation value; omitted qualifiers are unspecified, and no runtime reference is created.","not":"An assertion of state or location, a slicing operation, or a runtime object reference.","aliases":[]}

### S2 | type: add | dimension: member-family | symbol: descriptive_operations
- Needs: n1/n3 (t1:s1); n5 (t2:s2), n7 (t2:s4), n9 (t2:s6), n11 (t2:s8), n12 (t2:s10), n13 (t2:s12), n14 (t2:s14), n15 (t2:s16), n16 (t2:s18), n18 (t2:s20), n19 (t2:s22), n20 (t2:s24).
- Searches tried: search "describe requested action with arguments", "action description destination source direction distance", "ordered sequence of requested actions", "described procedure movement step count crossing room", "step forward left across room turn around"; widen "nonexecuting structured action description with operation-specific arguments", "cool a lettuce slice", "place object on the counter", "turn left and walk across the room to face the sink", "pick up the knife from the sink", "turn around and step forward to face the lettuce on the counter", "cut the lettuce on the counter into slices", "turn around and step forward to face the counter", "place the knife on the counter", "pick up a slice of lettuce from the counter", "turn around and step forward to face the fridge", "cool the lettuce slice in the fridge and remove it", "take a step to the left to face the counter", "place the lettuce slice on the counter to the right of the sink"; closest entries are executable chill/place/turn/walk/face/pick_up/slice/remove, activity (missing roles and reviewed verb interpretations), and sequence (orders descriptions but cannot supply them).
- Shared category rules: All eight members are primitive TERM constructors describing prospective or mentioned operations; none executes, asserts performance, acquires REF, supplies resources, or produces EVENT. Entity arguments are TERM descriptions including lexical_label; omissions are unspecified, not defaults. Existing operation definitions supply the operation's core interpretation, but these signatures are descriptive and intentionally allow unspecified resources.
- Members: describe_chill — reduce the target's temperature using an optional stated resource; describe_place — put the target at destination with optional placement and landmark relations; describe_pick_up — select/acquire the target from an optional source; describe_slice — cut target material into slices, not merely select sliced material; describe_remove — remove target from a source enclosure/container; describe_turn — rotate the agent relative to its current orientation; describe_walk — locomote toward a destination or with an explicit relative direction, step count or crossing path; describe_face — orient the agent body/view toward the target.
- Exceptions: For describe_turn, specify exactly one of angle or side; angle is degrees, 180 describes turning around without choosing clockwise versus counterclockwise, side is left_of or right_of interpreted as egocentric turn direction without specifying angular magnitude. For describe_walk, direction is in_front_of, behind, left_of or right_of interpreted respectively as forward, backward, leftward or rightward relative movement; steps is a positive integer counting footsteps; across identifies a traversed room/area and adds no length. Relations do not establish global compass orientation.
- Typed parameters: describe_chill(target: TERM, destination?: TERM); describe_place(target: TERM, destination: TERM, relation?: STRING, location?: TERM, location_relation?: STRING); describe_pick_up(target: TERM, source?: TERM); describe_slice(target: TERM); describe_remove(target: TERM, source?: TERM); describe_turn(angle?: NUMBER, side?: STRING); describe_walk(destination?: TERM, direction?: STRING, steps?: NUMBER, across?: TERM); describe_face(target: TERM); all return TERM.
- Interpretation: describe_place.relation locates target relative to destination (e.g. on counter); location/location_relation occur together and add a second landmark condition (e.g. right_of sink), not a replacement destination. describe_slice preserves the material description without fabricating the identity or count of resulting pieces. describe_chill with omitted destination encodes a cooling goal without inventing a fridge. Each other member preserves the corresponding operation's descriptive roles.
- Example: sequence of describe_turn(side=left_of), describe_walk(across=room_term, destination=sink_term), describe_face(target=sink_term) describes turning left and crossing the room to face the sink; describe_place(target=slice_term, destination=counter_term, relation=on, location=sink_term, location_relation=right_of) describes the final placement.
- Contrast: RECORD ACTION chill would report an occurrence, whereas describe_chill is merely the content of a request/proposal. A walk to a counter alone does not preserve an explicitly stated single leftward footstep.
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_chill","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_chill(target: TERM, destination?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes cooling target material, using destination as the cooling resource when supplied; target and destination are entity descriptions. Omitted destination is unspecified; no operation, success, object acquisition or thermal threshold is asserted.","not":"Selecting something already cold or recording completed cooling.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_place","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_place(target: TERM, destination: TERM, relation?: STRING, location?: TERM, location_relation?: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Describes placing the target entity at destination; relation is a spatial-relation locating target relative to destination. Optional location and location_relation must occur together and specify an additional spatial-relation between the placement site and a landmark; construction neither acquires nor moves an object.","not":"Dropping without a destination, or asserting a completed placement.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_pick_up","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_pick_up(target: TERM, source?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes selecting/acquiring the target entity, optionally from the stated source entity or location. Does not acquire a runtime reference or assert that the pickup occurred.","not":"A successful pickup event or an independently invented object selection.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_slice","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_slice(target: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes cutting target material into slices, preserving its tracked aggregate material identity without naming or counting the resulting pieces. Asserts no occurrence and supplies no unmentioned cutting instrument.","not":"Selecting already sliced material or claiming that slicing succeeded.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_remove","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_remove(target: TERM, source?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes removing target from an enclosure or container; optional source identifies that enclosure/container and omission leaves it unspecified. Neither executes the removal nor asserts that the target is already inside or outside.","not":"Deleting text or recording a completed removal.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_turn","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_turn(angle?: NUMBER, side?: STRING) -> TERM","definition":"Describes rotating the agent body/view relative to its current orientation; exactly one argument is required. angle is a nonnegative magnitude in degrees, with 180 meaning a reversal without a chosen rotational side; side must be left_of or right_of and denotes an egocentric left/right turn with unspecified angle.","not":"Translating leftward, tilting gaze, or inventing a compass bearing.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_walk","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_walk(destination?: TERM, direction?: STRING, steps?: NUMBER, across?: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes agent locomotion with at least one argument: destination is an entity/location description, steps is a positive integer counting footsteps, across is a traversed area description. direction is in_front_of/behind/left_of/right_of interpreted as egocentric forward/backward/leftward/rightward movement; omitted distance, direction and path are unspecified and no motion occurs.","not":"A body rotation, an automatic arrival claim, or a step count converted to an invented metric distance.","aliases":[]}
- Proposed record: {"symbol":"describe_face","kind":"constructor","signature":"TERM describe_face(target: TERM) -> TERM","definition":"Describes orienting agent body/view directly toward the perceptible target entity described by target. Does not imply walking to the target or assert completed orientation.","not":"Merely mentioning a topic or tilting the visual gaze.","aliases":[]}
